#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Runs the FAST tier of the frostvein gate before every commit.
#
# TIMING, re-measured 2026-09-08 because the figures below had gone stale by an order of
# magnitude: the fast tier is now 50-95 s (not ~5 s) and the full gate is ~530 s (not ~67 s).
# The ruling recorded below still holds -- fast on commit, heavy elsewhere -- but read its
# numbers as history, not as today's.
#
# ENABLE (once per clone):  git config core.hooksPath .githooks
#
# `.git/hooks/` is not versioned, so this lives in a tracked directory and is
# activated by that config line. `git commit --no-verify` still bypasses it —
# the point is to make green the default and skipping it a deliberate, visible
# act, not to make it impossible.
#
# WHY FAST HERE (2026-08-23, Wolf's ruling at the M2 retrospective): the full gate is
# ~67s and 88% of that is one daemon integration suite. 67s on every commit is clumsy
# enough to tempt `--no-verify`, and a gate that gets skipped protects nothing. The
# fast tier keeps fmt, clippy, the dependency-edge probes, the metrics tests, the
# mutation-table audit and every test EXCEPT crates/simd/tests/serve.rs.
#
# serve.rs runs at push instead — see .githooks/pre-push. It is not weakened, only moved.

exec "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/scripts/gate.sh" --fast
